WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.139 --> 00:00:04.660
Now that we've gone over Blueprints and UMG,

2
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:07.459
let's get started with our workshop.

3
00:00:07.459 --> 00:00:09.699
Now, the goals of this workshop is

4
00:00:09.699 --> 00:00:11.380
to create a simple driving game.

5
00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.460
We're going to implement a game time limit.

6
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.259
We'll build a reusable pickup objects.

7
00:00:15.259 --> 00:00:18.940
And we will create some UMG display and menus.

8
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:22.640
So again, we're going to make a full game loop,

9
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:23.420
if you will.

10
00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:25.339
And we're going to sprinkle in our UMG

11
00:00:25.339 --> 00:00:27.719
and show you how we can connect, but more importantly,

12
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.719
connect and talk to our UMG with our objects in our project.

13
00:00:31.719 --> 00:00:35.240
Now, to get us started, what I want everybody to do

14
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.520
is go ahead and create a new project

15
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.600
using the vehicle template.

16
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.960
Now, I'm using Unreal Engine 5.3.

17
00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.280
This tutorial has been updated in Reflex

18
00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.600
using that version of Unreal.

19
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:51.679
If you're using an earlier version

20
00:00:51.679 --> 00:00:54.640
or a future version of Unreal, please

21
00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.600
know if things don't work, try this in 5.3.

22
00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.840
And you should have success.

23
00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.840
Other things, again, we want the vehicle template right here.

24
00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:05.959
Also make sure that we have our starter content enabled.

25
00:01:05.959 --> 00:01:07.480
And go ahead and hit Create.

26
00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.400
And let's go ahead and open up that project

27
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.560
once that's done.
